  "_comment": "Category buckets for Set 18 augment ids (all DA_-prefixed), classified 2026-10-15 from Riot Data Dragon 16.20.1 tft-augments.json name+description text (249 DA_ augments), by the same method and boundaries as data/sets/set17/augments.json (read its _comment). Buckets are mutually exclusive, as in Set 17. Two passes: (1) 139 augments carry the same display name as a Set 17 augment that Set 17 curation already bucketed; each was compared against that augment's Data Dragon text and kept in the same bucket (56 have reworded text or changed numbers, none changed what they grant). (2) The other 110 were classified by hand: economy = the main reward is spendable gold and/or shop rerolls (incl. the Destiny augments and streak-setting, as in Set 17); items = grants a named item or uses generic item-grant language (component/anvil/emblem/artifact/radiant); units = grants a specific named champion (the Set 18 trait augments: \"Gain a Yunara, a Yorick, and a Karma\"), which wins over an item grant as in Set 17; combat = stats or combat effects only. Left unclassified by the Set 17 rule for generic random rewards: random-champion grants (Booster Pack, Champ Delivery, Worth the Wait, Kick Start, Build A Bud, ...), XP-only (Explosive Growth, Silver Spoon, Level Up, Clear Mind, Patient Study, Time Skip, Slammin as in Set 17), next-augment tier changes (Augmented Power), dice/chaos/egg rewards, champion duplicators alone (Team Building, Weight The Worth), and loot orbs (Bonus Gifts). Only economy and items are read by a checker today (AUGMENT_001, AUGMENT_004 via src/coach/checkers/augments.ts); units feeds augment-unit-grants.json through scripts/fetch-ddragon.js.",
